    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ed066ed9_18b0630c",
        "filename": "common/thermal.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1130551
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-19T04:57:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We are not disabling any capability here. Above is the if condition, under true EC controls the Fan else DPTF controls the fan. DPTF is thermal daemon in OS, it does all AP throttling (as Passive cooling) and emergency shutdown (as Critical policy) for safety action. DPTF also does Active cooling with Fan control at OS level for AP.",
      "parentUuid": "90b8c85a_deb29090",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 114,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "8180ad00db9ab207f50c3bc36e22b91c2aeff093",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d7a27d19_c0fe5dd3",
        "filename": "common/thermal.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-19T18:40:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you explain why we no longer need something external to DPTF (\u003dEC) to monitor the temperatures and throttle or shutdown AP? Why do we believe DPTF always functions soundly thus we can disable EC\u0027s fail-safe capability?",
      "parentUuid": "ed066ed9_18b0630c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 114,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "8180ad00db9ab207f50c3bc36e22b91c2aeff093",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "55d17036_e866a078",
        "filename": "common/thermal.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1127214
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-24T23:20:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Consolidating thermal monitoring/control and performance control in one place(DPTF) has advantages to implement more sophisticated system-wide policies, for example maximizing system performance while balancing cooling and fan noise...\nEC still reads on board\u0027s thermal sensors(another hook,\"thermal_control_dptf\"(dptf.c)) and informs thermal threshold event(threshold trip event) to DPTF.\nPROCHOT# is not necessary since DPTF initiates shutdown if too hot. \nEC based fail-safe \u0027still\u0027 exists and EC will take fan control over in case temperature is above threshold assuming that DPTF daemon is not working for some reason.",
      "parentUuid": "d7a27d19_c0fe5dd3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 114,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "8180ad00db9ab207f50c3bc36e22b91c2aeff093",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3606f8b8_353429d8",
        "filename": "common/thermal.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-24T23:56:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are you saying we don\u0027t need the code from line 193 through 219 when DPTF looks active?\n\nWhat grantees DPTF always functions soundly?",
      "parentUuid": "55d17036_e866a078",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 114,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "8180ad00db9ab207f50c3bc36e22b91c2aeff093",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4b828f76_1f5d72ef",
        "filename": "common/thermal.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1327490
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-25T00:42:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How can DPTF be a fail-safe if it\u0027s implemented as a software daemon in userspace?  The fail-safe in this case is not who controls the fan, it\u0027s who controls PROCHOT# and can force the chipset to shutdown to avoid damage.",
      "parentUuid": "3606f8b8_353429d8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 114,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "8180ad00db9ab207f50c3bc36e22b91c2aeff093",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a40ca9e_dd1bac03",
        "filename": "common/thermal.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1127214
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-25T01:34:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think \u0027fail-safe\u0027 give us lots of confusion. It means \u0027System-wide temperature/fan control fail-safe\u0027, not DPTF daemon itself to be fail-safe !)  \n\nLine 193 ~ 219 is unnecessary if DPTF is running in user space since DPTF does the job.\nIf DPTF is running normally, this \u0027thermal_control\u0027 thread(hook) is only for monitoring DPTF\u0027s health \u0027indirectly\u0027 by checking on-board temperature sensors.(line 110)  If temperature is above the threshold, it just assumes DPTF does not do its job and let EC to control fan(line 112).\nFan will be controlled regardless by either DPTF or EC. This is system wide fail-safe in fan control.  \n\nIf CPU temperature is too hot, DPTF will start shutdown process. if DPTF is down and CPU is getting hot, EC will notice and will control fan to cool CPU down. \nIf both DPTF and EC are down, we don\u0027t have solution. This will be same for system with NO DPTF and if EC is down, PROCHOT# cannot be asserted.",
      "parentUuid": "4b828f76_1f5d72ef",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 114,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "8180ad00db9ab207f50c3bc36e22b91c2aeff093",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f5fdd640_06e9428c",
        "filename": "common/thermal.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-29T19:46:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Again, if we return at line 114, we assume DPTF is all good as long as is_dptf_still_active returns true. My understanding is that DPTF can be misconfigured or can be malfunctioning even if is_dptf_still_active returns true.\n\nLine 193 ~ 219 are the mechanisms which can protect the board regardless the DPTF state or configuration.",
      "parentUuid": "4a40ca9e_dd1bac03",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 114,
